#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119610 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/id #uuid "9552ad30-9d46-5884-9877-18ca8842c252" :question/math-academy-id "e-4775" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b},$ given by\n![](images/f1/f1124e83e3b7614557a1a6de54523cc99f62ba2a52af1da8e4d22e14466ce020.svg)\nIf $\\langle x_1,x_2 \\rangle$ and $\\langle y_1,y_2 \\rangle$ are the solutions to the systems $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ and $L\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{b}$ respectively, what is the value of $x_1 \\cdot y_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/a1/a185a6fd91c78ed3e291b3ac8b99f9430290e5d8c1060a7d97317efc230aeb40.svg)\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/1e/1e780d384ca1fd957d742bbd047399c558ab016d187ce4cf71682546673aba35.svg)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=6 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=6$ and $y_2=4.$ Therefore, \n![](images/58/58da62903247cf6dfdf33be86293c181ef5184048ca7cd6c921360e5d202f353.svg)\n\n- Next, we solve $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/e0/e0563dde4944ecbe2ccb98bc91246fa18c7a808df96ab77f9f8efb5510084677.svg)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $x_2=-2$ and $x_1=2.$ Therefore, \n![](images/a8/a84088cff2a3589652ef7cabf09e3d8429fad7797ea20d44a416f85dcc7f9b65.svg)\n\nFinally, $x_1 \\cdot y_2 = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119611 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "24bc4954-462b-5066-83d4-8a4a87efc7b7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4777" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n![](images/a1/a13a7752a224bdabc27558a6a41e2b24d3c7918af1ca4d9cff802dcb54259238.svg)\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/60/605f569e0b4a54d2ca68d7b3330a2a0ebb06dcaba2b7efa911f58dbffd796fb0.svg)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n![](images/d2/d259a6740aa32e0e577756375fd85589b815232314511c74dc434a88d0146a3b.svg)\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4 \\\\ {y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =4-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =4-(2) \\\\  & =2, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1-(2)+2(2) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](images/c5/c5198aa83d3976d992b200f63941261f952282fedb241db780c20c12c97e3ba9.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119706 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cbefba9a-eda2-5a8e-8bb5-59ea4175b835" :question/math-academy-id "e-8926" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n\n![](images/9d/9d0b186213211813b290f502888f68e0603bc9f77bcd7ea9d6262cb7449c00e7.svg)\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/42/4298fe244fd6c66c7623ad508c97b96464321387506aa1e4be5e2399a5c9a862.svg)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 66\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ 15{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=5$ and $y_2=-9.$ \n\nTherefore, ![](images/a8/a86dfd0e07b8c415e526764cf9f7ba8f020609bf7b13cc90536deba868ec4aa6.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c72a1a6-e9cc-5dc7-8129-ca02b99a9f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478603} {:answer/id #uuid "204b0962-b138-56df-b0fd-2796efaabbe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478609} {:answer/id #uuid "81b0d9a3-f05e-52aa-baca-6aa189c65731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 49\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478756} {:answer/id #uuid "9043cde5-3c71-5771-9a3d-347775e2a488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -49\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478790} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9afe1b-bb2b-5925-8cb5-cfde20011076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9043cde5-3c71-5771-9a3d-347775e2a488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -49\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478790} :answer-field/id #uuid "db587132-2223-5d73-bd8b-93dbc82d6d91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb1f16a0-3031-5b97-a1fa-27b860c24df9" :question/math-academy-id "q-105753" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=9 \\\\ 11{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=9$ and ${y}_{2}=-49.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -49\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0043e87e-f842-57e6-82bc-b4ea7ec5f162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478563} {:answer/id #uuid "2e8f7d3a-59d4-56b1-9c28-1128e20099aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -78\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478632} {:answer/id #uuid "4856545f-c7b8-5207-946b-42bd4c1c3aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 64\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478660} {:answer/id #uuid "92afe7cc-d13c-59a1-b5db-5b37ab35d121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -50\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478798} {:answer/id #uuid "f363ef1a-e780-507a-81d1-0ea4237f7e39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 60\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0043e87e-f842-57e6-82bc-b4ea7ec5f162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478563} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b6940e4-bb59-563a-a937-e93f48ec1bc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88def0e2-16e4-59a7-96bb-d850c4ea1c49" :question/math-academy-id "q-105758" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=8 \\\\ -8{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=8$ and ${y}_{2}=50.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 50\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d4b3937-d636-543e-b0d6-739f7a00e7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238719} {:answer/id #uuid "59c3bb80-7b1c-535e-843c-7be8777981fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238826} {:answer/id #uuid "d6a16e65-a824-55dd-90aa-570d8ce9e4fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239931} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc1e9dc-6f28-50f2-90f2-765e57d990e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239972} {:answer/id #uuid "ec701eb0-1499-57d0-9f0b-83cacf08003b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d4b3937-d636-543e-b0d6-739f7a00e7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238719} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e2738a-d273-5c9d-8b63-8b44a8f24c45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3a99bb0-e72d-5183-bc18-0817eb820005" :question/math-academy-id "q-105760" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=7 \\\\ -10{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=7$ and ${y}_{2}=34.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e2d06e1-3417-5d35-8cf9-65a546979702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478692} {:answer/id #uuid "79133504-cdc8-50d1-aa34-0969c29bcf2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478738} {:answer/id #uuid "8fd1c199-45e5-5ea6-978f-4358accf0c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478787} {:answer/id #uuid "956543c5-8ef1-5bc5-846f-2b5c75aeb0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478804} {:answer/id #uuid "a10292bf-b579-5963-ba7f-90d1ac0490d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a10292bf-b579-5963-ba7f-90d1ac0490d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478821} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6844dfb-a5ce-580b-b6b3-0beb630d472c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e717653a-60c8-527b-b3b4-e108ff685e10" :question/math-academy-id "q-105932" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=3 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =3, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =1-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =1-(3) \\\\  & =-2, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-3-2{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-3-2(3)+2(-2) \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "253c5bec-a5e7-5fe4-8936-ee84f06ad2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 70 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238380} {:answer/id #uuid "3431ca67-1154-5315-a55d-30d8b6ec10fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -63 \\\\ 81\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238506} {:answer/id #uuid "5467b34d-2f1e-5c78-85dd-2b5382f7e7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238782} {:answer/id #uuid "b152e191-5d18-598f-a23e-0286d0d7f786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 56 \\\\ -80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239602} {:answer/id #uuid "c8674c02-d35b-548c-9f92-7fdac92d42e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -70 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5467b34d-2f1e-5c78-85dd-2b5382f7e7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238782} :answer-field/id #uuid "697b8f6f-9b78-510a-bdce-c0f202963523" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90586eea-75b4-50dc-8971-26e34a9a2816" :question/math-academy-id "q-105934" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=9 \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=7 \\\\ -9{y}_{1}+{y}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =9, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =7-7{y}_{1} \\\\  & =7-7(9) \\\\  & =-56, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-1+9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1+9(9) \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22f6367b-84f5-5b47-a09a-aa8de2644b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238362} {:answer/id #uuid "813327d9-1832-51ef-84d1-00133e2f63a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239176} {:answer/id #uuid "8e93b878-423d-5080-a191-f592c8e25cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{130}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239293} {:answer/id #uuid "b7069b81-e348-5968-b6ae-a411b5b35221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239649} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc34193-52f9-5bb0-a06a-5f9897960a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7069b81-e348-5968-b6ae-a411b5b35221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239649} :answer-field/id #uuid "54336a57-2806-5ed6-bb5d-a86bbfed1d7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68b89d00-e814-5d60-8ff8-bbe1b29f01fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-105953" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=14.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-7$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{26}{7}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{26}{7} \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=\\frac{26}{7}\\cdot 14=52.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title