d}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-2 \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-2$ and ${y}_{2}=5.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c66c0e-e0d0-5c27-907f-9e31b4c17877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478616} {:answer/id #uuid "44df3446-722a-5a1f-9400-f9c2edb4a1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478656} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b54213-3d59-59c8-98ef-a8f08dbb4c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478822} {:answer/id #uuid "d1de89e0-2dc2-5990-94a4-6e3067c9a319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478892} {:answer/id #uuid "e65b36d6-4ce8-57b8-a24e-fa7877ec664c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e65b36d6-4ce8-57b8-a24e-fa7877ec664c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478916} :answer-field/id #uuid "61c0b255-63a0-5164-9dd6-3298c1d228e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "084c02e4-7974-5581-92ae-668d0f97c0f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-107170" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ -3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=2$ and ${y}_{2}=4.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e232736-d49a-5bd9-b675-ee5259fec02e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478631} {:answer/id #uuid "815e68e7-ca75-58f1-bcfc-ed2da4282e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478754} {:answer/id #uuid "95cf673a-2ed5-5f8f-8bf1-3f41b9554c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478805} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e2561d-5010-5edc-889a-d78a29403e9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478829} {:answer/id #uuid "aadef4be-b14a-56bf-bbcb-88222c60c6ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e232736-d49a-5bd9-b675-ee5259fec02e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478631} :answer-field/id #uuid "48192aeb-3b0f-5497-bc1d-dd799e8a5dc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7099a838-c9d8-54d6-9fec-92d9fefe3598" :question/math-academy-id "q-107184" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}-3{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-4, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-5-2{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-5-2(-4) \\\\  & =3, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =9+4{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2} \\\\  & =9+4(-4)+3(3) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc9a6bd-a591-5999-b245-91b38db136b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478577} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed5ec33-0fac-5b1f-8846-71b9668a161a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478724} {:answer/id #uuid "a0981e4f-9bc7-5c90-b871-88aafbf5dc4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478820} {:answer/id #uuid "d358ce26-83c5-527a-b35c-94335a5980f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478894} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc58994-bee3-54d3-8345-6cff06c3be4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcc58994-bee3-54d3-8345-6cff06c3be4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478954} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d527114-1572-54ac-b766-1707893768e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ad4c6c3-50cf-5ba9-ae9f-35f5ce660c90" :question/math-academy-id "q-107497" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=1 \\\\ 9{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=1$ and ${y}_{2}=-3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 6{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{1}=-2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{1}=(-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot 1=-\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122c6d88-8494-5aec-a026-229428468b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377102} {:answer/id #uuid "a24fc545-7e28-5319-b8ea-0050a0425013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377103} {:answer/id #uuid "565b9eb2-7221-52ec-8a34-db861601dd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377104} {:answer/id #uuid "66cde035-3c2e-5045-8a57-e62cdfc4c320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377105} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec426d5-6612-5ded-909b-99d6a4c1702f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66cde035-3c2e-5045-8a57-e62cdfc4c320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377105} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4faae0-0911-57b4-a7e3-89f58f84a03e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf45deeb-ab83-510b-8f67-2f8280e43963" :question/math-academy-id "q-32543" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=1 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =1, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2+2{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2+2(1) \\\\  & =0, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =2+{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2+(1)-(0) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "032457e9-02bf-5ad6-9987-99a0689c6243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390759} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2b9196-139c-5abe-8bf3-f21b13bb615e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390760} {:answer/id #uuid "d6722917-7648-59db-8da1-966d52f9d9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390761} {:answer/id #uuid "9541c84f-6c02-5508-afe7-624da511dbdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390762} {:answer/id #uuid "749e40df-d35d-5ad6-9d4a-9737f8552554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad2b9196-139c-5abe-8bf3-f21b13bb615e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390760} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e79de7e-b384-5ea6-bb81-dfd5832cccb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b44ae0d1-f2bc-52f5-a02c-1e4fb0c1d4e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-32561" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=3 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=3$ and ${y}_{2}=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 3=-\\frac{9}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f0224fe-d8c2-5cc1-8f3c-e522430032e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{134}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478607} {:answer/id #uuid "49b907b6-2183-5755-bb06-f22146e37570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{188}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478664} {:answer/id #uuid "521a4a18-d5e1-5275-86bd-fd4d0bbb7613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478676} {:answer/id #uuid "9126f568-e746-57ed-bb73-ef7602c0d19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478792} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a94ece-2daa-5c37-8ecc-a6ffaebd161a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "521a4a18-d5e1-5275-86bd-fd4d0bbb7613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478676} :answer-field/id #uuid "d05942a2-78c5-5b8e-b7fc-65092edacbc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ab64b08c-fec6-5dff-b1cc-ff3d1f5e73c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32566" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of $\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=3 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=3$ and ${y}_{2}=-12.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-12$ and ${x}_{1}=-5.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be1af41-0c7e-535a-9a86-a5c82122dcdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300250} {:answer/id #uuid "89b9efd6-ce79-56d0-af07-0e42c41ffec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300659} {:answer/id #uuid "98709d57-b5d1-505c-a13b-2435f487b4d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300728} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fc1198-c5b8-53d4-8b4a-c8b8adf38ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300866} {:answer/id #uuid "b65d5146-dbe1-5221-b3af-8171d063039f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98709d57-b5d1-505c-a13b-2435f487b4d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300728} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff87f9e-a211-5118-b7af-25e270840e47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "74c73bef-8f9e-5d05-b33f-448bad8fb053" :question/math-academy-id "q-32570" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-4$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-4+3(-\\frac{2}{3})=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067598d2-ade2-5dd5-8073-c389ff24174b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478568} {:answer/id #uuid "1c178bab-1c92-5a25-ae64-df6277ac397a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478602} {:answer/id #uuid "3aea1048-26e5-56d0-bd6c-955510f59840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478642} {:answer/id #uuid "81992826-cc58-58c1-a7a5-01d46348c63f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478755} {:answer/id #uuid "a28f92ee-2682-564b-832c-3e2a4ecbc8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a28f92ee-2682-564b-832c-3e2a4ecbc8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478826} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d96da9c-3e97-52fd-92c9-c73ab85d4165" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53971d39-ffaa-5c20-9081-d54743d61b0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-32579" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=6 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2 \\\\ {y}_{1}-{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =6, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2+{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-(6)+4 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
